<title>NEW ZEALAND: FCL Paper turns in first half loss.</title>
<headline>FCL Paper turns in first half loss.</headline>
<dateline>AUCKLAND 1996-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half yr to Dec 31, 1996.</p>
<p>			   (million NZ$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss					40 vs 186 profit</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			 (loss) 9.9 vs profit 26.1</p>
<p>    Div (cents)				  3.0 vs same</p>
<p>    Turnover (billion)			1.91 vs 2.48</p>
<p>    Pretax loss				  162 vs profit 155</p>
<p>    Tax				    credit 12 vs debit 90</p>
<p>Dividend carries 1.48 cps imputation credit.</p>
<p>Pay date April 2</p>
<p>Reg date March 14  </p>
<p>Note - Fletcher Paper is the pulp and paper division of Fletcher Challenge Ltd. Market expectations were for a loss or a break-even result. Operating earnings included NZ$162 million in depreciation and $9.0 million in forest depletions.</p>
<p>Balance sheet (in billions unless stated)</p>
<p>    Current assets			    1.27 vs 1.66</p>
<p>    Total assets				6.74 vs 7.11</p>
<p>    Current liabilities		     0.93 vs 1.03</p>
<p>    Total liabilities			 3.12 vs 2.99</p>
<p>    Shareholders' equity		    1.39 vs 1.76</p>
<p>Cashflow from operating activities (million) 62 vs 196  </p>
<p>Cashflow from investing activities (million) (305) vs (226)</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 473-4746</p>
</text>
